            <span class="mk">How to read this</span>
            <p>Each panel is one industry's sixteen years of nominal value added, drawn to its own scale: the grid compares trajectories, not sizes; the printed share does the sizing. The top row is heavy industry and process plants: metals, vehicles, chemicals, food, pharmaceuticals. The famous labour-intensive exporters, textiles, apparel, leather, sit far down the shelf, large in employment and modest in value added.</p>
            <p>Nominal caution applies panel by panel: a rising line is prices as much as product. The shapes still discriminate: some industries dip in 2020-21 and snap back, others never quite do.</p>
