            <p>The value-added grid above ranks industries by money; this strip ranks the same industries by people. The two rankings do not agree. Textiles, apparel and food, the classic labour-intensive trades, climb to the top here while sitting far down the value shelf. Basic metals and chemicals, the value leaders, carry fewer people than their rupee share implies.</p>
