            <span class="dl"><button data-dl="svg">SVG</button><span class="sep"></span><button data-dl="png">PNG</button><span class="sep"></span><button data-dl="csv">CSV</button><span class="sep"></span><a href="https://www.mospi.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Source ↗</a></span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="explain">
          <div class="ev">
            <span class="mk">How to read this</span>
            <p>The Factories Act starts counting at ten workers with power, twenty without, so even the smallest unit here is a real workplace. Car plants, electronics assembly and pharmaceuticals run large shifts under one roof. Rice mills, sawmills and cotton gins are small and scattered. Put this plate next to the one above and size and pay do not line up: bidi and garment factories are large and pay the least, while refineries are middling in size and pay the most. What a job pays follows the machines behind each worker more than the headcount around them.</p>
