  <!-- § 07 the other economy -->
  <section>
    <div class="sec-head"><span class="no">09</span><h2>The other economy, counted at last</h2><span class="line"></span><span class="unit">ASUSE, establishments, ₹ per year</span></div>
    <p>ASUSE, the Annual Survey of Unincorporated Sector Enterprises, is the young counterpart to the ASI's old ledger. It counts establishments no factory inspector visits: the tailor, the tea stall, the two-room workshop. The survey splits them in two. An <b>own-account establishment</b> (OAE) hires nobody: usually one person, or a family, working for themselves. A <b>hired-worker establishment</b> (HWE) employs at least one person for pay. In 2023-24 the own-account kind was <b id="ot-oaesh">–</b> of all establishments; the hired-worker kind, <b id="ot-hwesh">–</b>, held <b id="ot-hwewk">–</b> of the workers.</p>

    <div class="break basket" style="margin-top:44px">
      <div class="bar" id="bar-est"></div>
      <div class="labels" id="lab-est"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="break basket" style="margin-top:36px">
      <div class="bar" id="bar-wrk"></div>
      <div class="labels" id="lab-wrk"></div>
      <p class="note" id="note-q">A quarterly ASUSE bulletin began with {qFirst}. It is {uq.dates.length} quarters old: a reading of scale, not yet of trend: <b id="q-now">–</b> establishments counted in {qNow}{qPrev ? <Fragment>, against <b id="q-then">–</b> in {qPrev}</Fragment> : ""}. We read the level and wait.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="break" style="margin-top:104px">
      <figure id="cb-mult" style="margin:0">
        <div class="plate-head">
          <div class="t">
            <h3>One scale, two economies</h3>
            <div class="sub">Gross value added per worker, ₹ lakh per year, nominal, 2023-24, ASI derived vs ASUSE published</div>
          </div>
          <div class="plate-val"><div class="v" id="pv-mult">–</div><div class="c">factory ÷ unincorporated, 2023-24</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="frame">
          <div class="plotzone" id="plot-mult"></div>
          <div class="plotfoot">
            <span class="src">Source: MoSPI, factory bar derived: ASI GVA ÷ persons engaged, ASUSE bars published per-worker GVA, market establishments, both nominal, same year, never one survey</span>
            <span class="dl"><button data-dl="svg">SVG</button><span class="sep"></span><button data-dl="png">PNG</button><span class="sep"></span><button data-dl="csv">CSV</button><span class="sep"></span><a href="https://www.mospi.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Source ↗</a></span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="explain">
          <div class="ev">
            <span class="mk">How to read this</span>
            <p>This is the guide's one picture worth arguing about. A year of work in a registered factory yields several times the value added of a year in an unincorporated establishment. The gap is real, and it is not a verdict on the people: the factory worker stands next to machines, capital and scale that the shop worker does not have, in industries the shop cannot enter. The bars measure the establishment, not the person in it.</p>
            <p>Read the two grey bars against each other too: even inside the informal economy, an establishment that hires at all adds roughly double per head what an own-account one does. Hiring one person is India's steepest step up.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="now">
            <span class="mk">As of 2023-24</span>
            <p>Factory GVA per person engaged: <b id="ex-x1">–</b> a year. Unincorporated, all establishments: <b id="ex-x2">–</b>: a multiple of <b id="ex-x3">–</b>, rising to <b id="ex-x4">–</b> against own-account establishments alone. Pay tells the softer version: factory emoluments per head are <b id="ex-x5">–</b> against <b id="ex-x6">–</b> per hired worker in the informal economy: <b id="ex-x7">–</b>, not eight.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div class="break" style="margin-top:104px">
      <figure id="cb-sec" style="margin:0">
        <div class="plate-head">
          <div class="t">
            <h3>The shape of the informal economy</h3>
            <div class="sub">Workers and GVA per worker by broad activity &amp; sector, rural (grey) → urban (blue), 2023-24, ASUSE</div>
          </div>
          <div class="plate-val"><div class="v" id="pv-sec">–</div><div class="c">rural share of informal establishments, 2023-24</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="frame">
          <div class="legend">
            <button class="chip"><i style="background:#5F6675"></i>Rural</button>
            <button class="chip"><i style="background:#2E4BD8"></i>Urban</button>
          </div>
