          <div class="ev">
            <span class="mk">How to read this</span>
            <p>Much informal work done by women happens at home: rolling bidis, stitching garments on piece rates, weaving, running a tuition class from the verandah. Work outside the home, on the road or in the repair shop, is almost entirely men's. The survey counts a woman as a worker in an enterprise only if she works in it; women who work on the family farm or only at home for the household are outside this count altogether.</p>
