            <p>Everything monetary is nominal, and the sparklines mostly rise for that reason alone. The exceptions earn attention: a line that falls in nominal terms, rent paid for fixed assets, unpaid family members working in factories, fell in fact. One line is missing by design: the children-workers indicator is served only as a single corrupt row and is quarantined, not printed; 56 of the 57 lines are here.</p>
