  <footer class="provenance">
    <h2 class="prov-h">Sources, method and revisions</h2>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h6>Source of record</h6>
        <p>Ministry of Statistics &amp; Programme Implementation, National Statistical Office. Annual Survey of Industries, four classification blocks, NIC-1987 (1992-93 to 1997-98; 1993-94 not served by the source), NIC-1998 (1998-99 to 2003-04), NIC-2004 (2004-05 to 2007-08) and NIC-2008 (2008-09 to 2023-24), kept as four separate series, never spliced. ASUSE annual rounds 2021-22 to 2023-24, the calendar-year 2025 round (a separate series), and the quarterly bulletin from {qFirst} to {qNow}; every published ASUSE table is in the downloads, its full cross of state, sector, activity and establishment type held for the Atlas's deep archive. Retrieved via the eSankhyiki API, vintage <b id="prov-vintage">–</b>.</p>
        <p>Coverage: all 57 indicators the ASI 2008 block publishes are ingested raw, and 56 are baked (§10 carries the ledger; the children-workers indicator exists in the API only as a single corrupt row, its 2023-24 value duplicates the contract-workers count, and is quarantined, disclosed here and in the baked file); the older blocks publish 57, 28 and 32 indicators respectively, of which the comparable core is baked. Of ASUSE's 35 catalogued annual indicators, 20 are baked: the headline counts and rupee rates, the owner, paperwork and rhythm distributions (§09), and lean state cuts of establishments, workers and GVA per worker. The rest are state-wise duplicates of the All-India distributions (11 indicators) or minor residuals (multi-activity counts, internet-use types, size-band characteristics, worker types): skipped knowingly, listed in data/sources.yml.</p>
        <p>ASI monetary values are published in ₹ lakh and are shown here in ₹ lakh crore, nominal, with no deflation. The 1987 block serves Total Emoluments with a blank unit; it is ₹ lakh and is corrected and disclosed in the baked file. The 2010-11 sampling-frame revision is carried as published and annotated wherever a series crosses it. Ladakh's factory GVA is negative in 2021-22: a real published value, inputs exceeding output, not an error. Telangana appears from 2012-13 and Ladakh from 2019-20; earlier cells are null, not zero.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Revisions &amp; uncertainty</h6>
        <p>ASI and ASUSE results are final on release. The two surveys have different frames, units and histories and are shown side by side, never spliced or summed. ASUSE 2023-24 publishes per-hired-worker figures for hired-worker establishments only; the all-establishment variants end at 2022-23 and carry a disclosed trailing null.</p>
        <p>ASUSE quarterly counts are published in hundreds and converted for display. Where something is not measured, the informal economy before 2021-22, real factory output, this guide says "we do not know" rather than inventing a number.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>This guide</h6>
        <p>Enterprises, version 1.2, adds the labour-share-by-industry strip (§07), the ASUSE sectoral-structure dumbbell (§08) and the ASUSE state-dispersion strip (§08). Next scheduled revision: on release of either survey's next round.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
